-- scja2-part6-officers.l4: Part 6 (Officers and offices), ss 61 to 72: the Registrar, the Sheriff, the Accountant, subordinate officers, commissioners for oaths, oaths of office, the Registry.
-- Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 1 July 2024.
-- The source is a plain-text rendering (SCJA1969.txt), not the official text. Layer 1: the law, objectively; every name begins with the label of its provision.
-- JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act gives in its own words; NOTHING means the Act does not answer on these facts (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (scja2)").
-- The Legal Profession Act 1966 and the Police Force Act 2004 are not among the sources; borrowed facts are plain inputs.

§ `Part 6 -- Officers and offices`

§§ `Division 1 -- Registrar`

-- src:4065 | 61.—(1) The President may, on the recommendation of the Chief
-- src:4066 | Justice, appoint a Registrar, a Deputy Registrar and Assistant
-- src:4067 | Registrars of the Supreme Court.
@ref s 61(1) (src:4065-4067)
GIVEN officer IS A `Officer of the Supreme Court`
      `the Chief Justice recommends it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61(1) the President may appoint the officer of the Supreme Court` MEANS
    CONSIDER officer
    WHEN Registrar THEN `s 61(1) the President may appoint: the recommendation` `the Chief Justice recommends it`
    WHEN `Deputy Registrar` THEN `s 61(1) the President may appoint: the recommendation` `the Chief Justice recommends it`
    WHEN `Assistant Registrar` THEN `s 61(1) the President may appoint: the recommendation` `the Chief Justice recommends it`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is about a Registrar, a Deputy Registrar and Assistant Registrars; the other officers are dealt with elsewhere
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN recommended IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61(1) the President may appoint: the recommendation` recommended MEANS
    IF recommended
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The President may, on the recommendation of the Chief Justice, appoint" -- the "on the recommendation" is not met
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4069 | (2) A person must not be appointed to be or to act as the Registrar,
-- src:4070 | the Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar unless he or she is a
-- src:4071 | qualified person as defined in section 2 of the Legal Profession
-- src:4072 | Act 1966.
@ref s 61(2) (src:4069-4072)
GIVEN `the person is a qualified person as defined in section 2 of the Legal Profession Act 1966` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61(2) the person may be appointed to be or to act as the Registrar, the Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar` MEANS
    IF `the person is a qualified person as defined in section 2 of the Legal Profession Act 1966`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless" -- the unless is met, which lifts the bar, but the subsection does not itself grant the appointment, which is for section 61(1)
    THEN NOTHING
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person must not be appointed to be or to act as the Registrar, the Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar unless he or she is a qualified person"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4069 | (2) A person must not be appointed to be or to act as the Registrar,
-- src:4070 | the Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar unless he or she is a
-- src:4071 | qualified person as defined in section 2 of the Legal Profession
-- src:4072 | Act 1966.
@ref s 61(2) (src:4069-4072)
GIVEN `the person is a qualified person as defined in section 2 of the Legal Profession Act 1966` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61(2) the bar on appointing the person to be or to act as the Registrar, the Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar applies` MEANS
    IF `the person is a qualified person as defined in section 2 of the Legal Profession Act 1966`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless he or she is a qualified person as defined in section 2 of the Legal Profession Act 1966" -- the unless is met, so the bar is lifted
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 62 -- Powers and duties of Registrar, Deputy Registrar and Assistant Registrars`

-- src:4077 | 62.—(1) The Registrar, the Deputy Registrar and the Assistant
-- src:4078 | Registrars have, subject to the provisions of this Act or any other
-- src:4079 | written law, such jurisdiction, powers and duties as may be prescribed
-- src:4080 | by Rules of Court.
@ref s 62(1) (src:4077-4080)
GIVEN `the jurisdiction, power or duty is prescribed by Rules of Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62(1) the Registrar, the Deputy Registrar and the Assistant Registrars have the jurisdiction, power or duty` MEANS
    IF `the jurisdiction, power or duty is prescribed by Rules of Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the jurisdiction, powers and duties are those "prescribed by Rules of Court", which are not among the sources, and the subsection is "subject to the provisions of this Act or any other written law"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4082 | (2) Subject to Rules of Court, all the powers and duties conferred
-- src:4083 | and imposed on the Registrar may be exercised or performed by the
-- src:4084 | Deputy Registrar or the Assistant Registrars.
@ref s 62(2) (src:4082-4084)
GIVEN officer IS A `Officer of the Supreme Court`
      `Rules of Court provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62(2) the officer may exercise or perform the powers and duties conferred and imposed on the Registrar` MEANS
    CONSIDER officer
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to Rules of Court" -- where the Rules provide otherwise this subsection says nothing further
    WHEN `Deputy Registrar` THEN IF `Rules of Court provide otherwise` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to Rules of Court" -- where the Rules provide otherwise this subsection says nothing further
    WHEN `Assistant Registrar` THEN IF `Rules of Court provide otherwise` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is about the Deputy Registrar and the Assistant Registrars
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Division 2 -- Sheriff`

§§ `s 63 -- Sheriff, Deputy Sheriff and Assistant Sheriffs of Supreme Court`

-- src:4093 | 63.—(1) The Registrar is the Sheriff and the Deputy Registrar is the
-- src:4094 | Deputy Sheriff and the Assistant Registrars are the Assistant Sheriffs
-- src:4095 | of the Supreme Court.
@ref s 63(1) (src:4093-4095)
GIVEN officer IS A `Officer of the Supreme Court`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Officer of the Supreme Court`
`s 63(1) the office of the Sheriff that the officer holds` officer MEANS
    CONSIDER officer
    WHEN Registrar THEN JUST Sheriff
    WHEN `Deputy Registrar` THEN JUST `Deputy Sheriff`
    WHEN `Assistant Registrar` THEN JUST `Assistant Sheriff`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection names three offices and does not say that no other officer is a Sheriff
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:4093 | 63.—(1) The Registrar is the Sheriff and the Deputy Registrar is the
-- src:4094 | Deputy Sheriff and the Assistant Registrars are the Assistant Sheriffs
-- src:4095 | of the Supreme Court.
@ref s 63(1) (src:4093-4095)
GIVEN officer IS A `Officer of the Supreme Court`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63(1) the officer is a Sheriff, Deputy Sheriff or Assistant Sheriff of the Supreme Court` MEANS
    CONSIDER officer
    WHEN Registrar THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Deputy Registrar` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Assistant Registrar` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection names three offices and does not say that no other officer is a Sheriff
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:4097 | (2) The Deputy Sheriff and the Assistant Sheriffs have all the
-- src:4098 | powers and privileges and may perform all the duties of the Sheriff.
@ref s 63(2) (src:4097-4098)
GIVEN officer IS A `Officer of the Supreme Court`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63(2) the officer has all the powers and privileges and may perform all the duties of the Sheriff` MEANS
    CONSIDER officer
    WHEN `Deputy Sheriff` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Assistant Sheriff` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is about the Deputy Sheriff and the Assistant Sheriffs
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 64 -- Powers and duties of Sheriff`

DECLARE `s 64(1) party` IS ONE OF `s 64(1) the Sheriff or the Sheriff's officer`
DECLARE `s 64(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 64(1)(a) executes the process of the Supreme Court given to the Sheriff by the Court for that purpose`
    `s 64(1)(b) makes a return of the process together with the manner of its execution to the Supreme Court from which it issued`
    `s 64(1)(c) receives a person committed to the Sheriff's custody by the Supreme Court`

-- src:4109 | (a) execute all writs, summonses, rules, orders, warrants,
-- src:4110 | commands and process of the Supreme Court given to him
-- src:4111 | or her by the Court for that purpose;
@ref s 64(1)(a) (src:4109-4111)
GIVEN `the process was given to the Sheriff by the Supreme Court for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64(1)(a) the Sheriff or the Sheriff's officer must execute the process` MEANS
    IF `the process was given to the Sheriff by the Supreme Court for that purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is to execute process "given to him or her by the Court for that purpose"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4113 | (b) make a return of the same together with the manner of the
-- src:4114 | execution thereof to the Supreme Court from which the
-- src:4115 | process issued; and
@ref s 64(1)(b) (src:4113-4115)
GIVEN `the process issued from the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64(1)(b) the Sheriff or the Sheriff's officer must make a return of the process and the manner of its execution` MEANS
    IF `the process issued from the Supreme Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the return is made "to the Supreme Court from which the process issued"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4117 | (c) receive all persons committed to his or her custody by the
-- src:4118 | Supreme Court.
@ref s 64(1)(c) (src:4117-4118)
GIVEN `the person was committed to the Sheriff's custody by the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64(1)(c) the Sheriff or the Sheriff's officer must receive the person` MEANS
    IF `the person was committed to the Sheriff's custody by the Supreme Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is to receive persons "committed to his or her custody by the Supreme Court"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4107 | 64.—(1) The Sheriff or his or her officers must —
-- src:4109 | (a) execute all writs, summonses, rules, orders, warrants,
-- src:4110 | commands and process of the Supreme Court given to him
-- src:4111 | or her by the Court for that purpose;
-- src:4113 | (b) make a return of the same together with the manner of the
-- src:4114 | execution thereof to the Supreme Court from which the
-- src:4115 | process issued; and
-- src:4117 | (c) receive all persons committed to his or her custody by the
-- src:4118 | Supreme Court.
@ref s 64(1) (src:4107-4118)
`s 64(1)(a) and (b) the duty of the Sheriff to execute the process and make a return` MEANS
    PARTY `s 64(1) the Sheriff or the Sheriff's officer`
    MUST `s 64(1)(a) executes the process of the Supreme Court given to the Sheriff by the Court for that purpose`
    HENCE (
        PARTY `s 64(1) the Sheriff or the Sheriff's officer`
        MUST `s 64(1)(b) makes a return of the process together with the manner of its execution to the Supreme Court from which it issued`
        LEST BREACH BY `s 64(1) the Sheriff or the Sheriff's officer` BECAUSE "no return of the process was made to the Supreme Court"
    )
    LEST BREACH BY `s 64(1) the Sheriff or the Sheriff's officer` BECAUSE "the process given to the Sheriff by the Court was not executed"

#TRACE `s 64(1)(a) and (b) the duty of the Sheriff to execute the process and make a return` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 64(1) the Sheriff or the Sheriff's officer` DOES `s 64(1)(a) executes the process of the Supreme Court given to the Sheriff by the Court for that purpose` AT 1
    PARTY `s 64(1) the Sheriff or the Sheriff's officer` DOES `s 64(1)(b) makes a return of the process together with the manner of its execution to the Supreme Court from which it issued` AT 2

-- the same duty with the return not yet made: the text fixes no time for it, so the obligation stays pending (a residual obligation, not a breach)
#TRACE `s 64(1)(a) and (b) the duty of the Sheriff to execute the process and make a return` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 64(1) the Sheriff or the Sheriff's officer` DOES `s 64(1)(a) executes the process of the Supreme Court given to the Sheriff by the Court for that purpose` AT 1

-- src:4117 | (c) receive all persons committed to his or her custody by the
-- src:4118 | Supreme Court.
@ref s 64(1)(c) (src:4117-4118)
`s 64(1)(c) the duty of the Sheriff to receive the persons committed to the Sheriff's custody` MEANS
    PARTY `s 64(1) the Sheriff or the Sheriff's officer`
    MUST `s 64(1)(c) receives a person committed to the Sheriff's custody by the Supreme Court`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 64(1) the Sheriff or the Sheriff's officer` BECAUSE "the person committed to the Sheriff's custody by the Supreme Court was not received"

#TRACE `s 64(1)(c) the duty of the Sheriff to receive the persons committed to the Sheriff's custody` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 64(1) the Sheriff or the Sheriff's officer` DOES `s 64(1)(c) receives a person committed to the Sheriff's custody by the Supreme Court` AT 1

-- src:4120 | (2) The Sheriff or his or her officers in executing any enforcement
-- src:4121 | order for seizure and sale of property, any other enforcement order or
-- src:4122 | any writ of distress may effect an entry into any building, and for that
-- src:4123 | purpose if necessary may break open any outer or inner door or
-- src:4124 | window of the building or any receptacle therein, using such force as
-- src:4125 | is reasonably necessary to effect an entry.
@ref s 64(2) (src:4120-4125)
GIVEN `the Sheriff or the Sheriff's officer is executing an enforcement order for seizure and sale of property, another enforcement order or a writ of distress` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64(2) the Sheriff or the Sheriff's officer may effect an entry into the building` MEANS
    IF `the Sheriff or the Sheriff's officer is executing an enforcement order for seizure and sale of property, another enforcement order or a writ of distress`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is given "in executing" an enforcement order or a writ of distress
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4120 | (2) The Sheriff or his or her officers in executing any enforcement
-- src:4121 | order for seizure and sale of property, any other enforcement order or
-- src:4122 | any writ of distress may effect an entry into any building, and for that
-- src:4123 | purpose if necessary may break open any outer or inner door or
-- src:4124 | window of the building or any receptacle therein, using such force as
-- src:4125 | is reasonably necessary to effect an entry.
@ref s 64(2) (src:4120-4125)
GIVEN `the Sheriff or the Sheriff's officer is executing an enforcement order for seizure and sale of property, another enforcement order or a writ of distress` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is necessary for the purpose of effecting an entry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the force used is no more than is reasonably necessary to effect an entry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64(2) the Sheriff or the Sheriff's officer may break open any outer or inner door or window of the building or any receptacle therein` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is given "in executing" an enforcement order or a writ of distress
        IF NOT `the Sheriff or the Sheriff's officer is executing an enforcement order for seizure and sale of property, another enforcement order or a writ of distress` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for that purpose if necessary may break open" -- it is not necessary
        IF NOT `it is necessary for the purpose of effecting an entry` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the force used is no more than is reasonably necessary to effect an entry` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "using such force as is reasonably necessary to effect an entry" -- more force is outside the grant, which does not say in terms that it is forbidden
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 64(3) kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `s 64(3) an auxiliary police officer appointed under the Police Force Act 2004`
    `s 64(3) a security agency`
    `s 64(3) a provider of transport and of warehousing`
    `s 64(3) a valuer`
    `s 64(3) an estate agent`
    `s 64(3) a broker`
    `s 64(3) a solicitor`
    `s 64(3) any other person`

-- src:4129 | (3) The Sheriff may engage any auxiliary police officer appointed
-- src:4130 | under the Police Force Act 2004*, any security agency, a provider of
-- src:4131 | transport and of warehousing, a valuer, an estate agent, a broker, a
-- src:4132 | solicitor or any other appropriate person to assist the Sheriff in the
-- src:4133 | discharge of the Sheriff’s duties.
@ref s 64(3) (src:4129-4133)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 64(3) kind of person`
      `the person is an appropriate person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64(3) the Sheriff may engage the person to assist the Sheriff in the discharge of the Sheriff's duties` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 64(3) any other person` THEN
        IF `the person is an appropriate person`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any other appropriate person" -- a person who is not appropriate is outside the grant
        ELSE NOTHING
    -- the seven named kinds are listed without any condition
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 65 -- Sheriff not to act when an interested party`

-- src:4141 | 65. Where in any cause or matter the Sheriff is an interested party,
-- src:4142 | the court may appoint for that purpose an officer or a person who may
-- src:4143 | act in the place of the Sheriff.
@ref s 65 (src:4141-4143)
GIVEN `the Sheriff is an interested party in the cause or matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65 the court may appoint an officer or a person to act in the place of the Sheriff` MEANS
    IF `the Sheriff is an interested party in the cause or matter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where in any cause or matter the Sheriff is an interested party, the court may appoint" -- the "where" is not met
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 65A -- Solicitor authorised to act as officer of Sheriff`

DECLARE `s 65A(1) kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `s 65A(1) a solicitor`
    `s 65A(1) a person employed by a solicitor`
    `s 65A(1) another person`

-- src:4147 | 65A.—(1) Subject to such directions as may be given by the Chief
-- src:4148 | Justice, the Registrar may authorise a solicitor or a person employed
-- src:4149 | by a solicitor to exercise the powers and perform the duties of an
-- src:4150 | officer of the Sheriff during such period or on such occasion as the
-- src:4157 | Registrar thinks fit and subject to such terms and conditions as the
-- src:4158 | Registrar may determine.
@ref s 65A(1) (src:4147-4158)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 65A(1) kind of person`
      `the Chief Justice has given a direction that stands in the way` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65A(1) the Registrar may authorise the person to exercise the powers and perform the duties of an officer of the Sheriff` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Registrar may authorise "a solicitor or a person employed by a solicitor"; the subsection does not say in terms that no one else may be authorised
    WHEN `s 65A(1) another person` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the Chief Justice has given a direction that stands in the way`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to such directions as may be given by the Chief Justice" -- the direction prevails and the subsection says nothing further
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:4160 | (2) Section 79(2) applies to a solicitor or person authorised under
-- src:4161 | subsection (1) as it applies to an officer of the Supreme Court.
@ref s 65A(2) (src:4160-4161)
GIVEN `the person is a solicitor or person authorised under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 79(2) the officer is not liable to be sued` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65A(2) the solicitor or person authorised under subsection (1) is not liable to be sued` MEANS
    IF `the person is a solicitor or person authorised under subsection (1)`
    -- the answer of section 79(2) for an officer of the Supreme Court is the answer here (PLAN.md seam 17)
    THEN `s 79(2) the officer is not liable to be sued`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is about "a solicitor or person authorised under subsection (1)"
    ELSE NOTHING

