§§ `Division 4 -- Subordinate officers`

§§ `s 67 -- Subordinate officers of Supreme Court`

-- src:4184 | 67.—(1) There are to be attached to the Supreme Court
-- src:4185 | commissioners for oaths, interpreters, clerks, process servers and
-- src:4186 | other officers as, from time to time, appear to the Chief Justice to be
-- src:4187 | necessary for the administration of justice and the due execution of all
-- src:4188 | powers and duties which are vested in the Supreme Court.
@ref s 67(1) (src:4184-4188)
GIVEN officer IS A `Officer of the Supreme Court`
      `the officer appears to the Chief Justice to be necessary for the administration of justice and the due execution of the powers and duties vested in the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 67(1) officers of that kind are to be attached to the Supreme Court` MEANS
    CONSIDER officer
    -- fork F67-1: the four named kinds are read as attached without the condition; only "other officers as ... appear to the Chief Justice to be necessary" carry it
    WHEN `Commissioner for oaths` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN Interpreter THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN Clerk THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Process server` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Another officer of the Supreme Court` THEN
        IF `the officer appears to the Chief Justice to be necessary for the administration of justice and the due execution of the powers and duties vested in the Supreme Court`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "other officers as, from time to time, appear to the Chief Justice to be necessary"
        ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Registrar, the Sheriff and the Accountant have their own Divisions; this subsection speaks of the officers it names and of "other officers"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:4190 | (2) Those of the officers attached to the Supreme Court as may be
-- src:4191 | thought necessary or proper for the performance of any special duties
-- src:4192 | in connection with any particular Judge may, with the approval of the
-- src:4193 | Chief Justice, be attached to that Judge.
@ref s 67(2) (src:4190-4193)
GIVEN `the officer is thought necessary or proper for the performance of special duties in connection with the particular Judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Chief Justice approves` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 67(2) the officer may be attached to that Judge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is about "those of the officers ... as may be thought necessary or proper for the performance of any special duties in connection with any particular Judge"
        IF NOT `the officer is thought necessary or proper for the performance of special duties in connection with the particular Judge` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the Chief Justice approves` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, with the approval of the Chief Justice, be attached to that Judge" -- there is no approval
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 68 -- Commissioners for oaths`

-- src:4197 | 68.—(1) The Registrar, the Deputy Registrar and the Assistant
-- src:4198 | Registrars are ex-officio commissioners for oaths.
@ref s 68(1) (src:4197-4198)
GIVEN officer IS A `Officer of the Supreme Court`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 68(1) the officer is an ex-officio commissioner for oaths` MEANS
    CONSIDER officer
    WHEN Registrar THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Deputy Registrar` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Assistant Registrar` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection names three offices and does not say that no other officer is a commissioner for oaths ex officio
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:4205 | (2) The Senate of the Singapore Academy of Law may appoint fit
-- src:4206 | and proper persons to be commissioners for oaths (subject to any
-- src:4207 | limitations expressed in their appointment) who may do all or any of
-- src:4208 | the following things:
-- src:4210 | (a) receive acknowledgements of married women in all cases
-- src:4211 | where such acknowledgements are required by law to be
-- src:4212 | taken before a public officer;
-- src:4214 | (b) receive acknowledgements of recognisances of bail and
-- src:4215 | bail bonds;
-- src:4217 | (c) administer oaths for —
-- src:4219 | (i) the justification for bail;
-- src:4221 | (ii) taking any affidavit or affirmation;
-- src:4223 | (iii) receiving and taking the answer, plea, demurrer,
-- src:4224 | disclaimer, allegation or examination of any party or
-- src:4225 | parties to any action;
-- src:4227 | (iv) the examination of any witnesses upon any
-- src:4228 | interrogatories or de bene esse or in chief or on
-- src:4229 | any other occasions;
-- src:4231 | (v) swearing executors and administrators; and
-- src:4233 | (vi) swearing persons in any cause or matter which is
-- src:4234 | pending or about to be instituted in any court in any
-- src:4235 | of its jurisdiction;
-- src:4237 | (d) take and receive statutory declarations.
@ref s 68(2) (src:4205-4237)
GIVEN `the person is a fit and proper person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 68(2) the Senate of the Singapore Academy of Law may appoint the person to be a commissioner for oaths` MEANS
    IF `the person is a fit and proper person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Senate "may appoint fit and proper persons"; a person who is not one is outside the grant
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 68(2) thing a commissioner for oaths may do` IS ONE OF
    `s 68(2)(a) receive acknowledgements of married women in all cases where such acknowledgements are required by law to be taken before a public officer`
    `s 68(2)(b) receive acknowledgements of recognisances of bail and bail bonds`
    `s 68(2)(c)(i) administer oaths for the justification for bail`
    `s 68(2)(c)(ii) administer oaths for taking any affidavit or affirmation`
    `s 68(2)(c)(iii) administer oaths for receiving and taking the answer, plea, demurrer, disclaimer, allegation or examination of any party or parties to any action`
    `s 68(2)(c)(iv) administer oaths for the examination of any witnesses upon any interrogatories or de bene esse or in chief or on any other occasions`
    `s 68(2)(c)(v) administer oaths for swearing executors and administrators`
    `s 68(2)(c)(vi) administer oaths for swearing persons in any cause or matter which is pending or about to be instituted in any court in any of its jurisdiction`
    `s 68(2)(d) take and receive statutory declarations`
    `s 68(2) another thing`

-- src:4205 | (2) The Senate of the Singapore Academy of Law may appoint fit
-- src:4206 | and proper persons to be commissioners for oaths (subject to any
-- src:4207 | limitations expressed in their appointment) who may do all or any of
-- src:4208 | the following things:
-- src:4210 | (a) receive acknowledgements of married women in all cases
-- src:4211 | where such acknowledgements are required by law to be
-- src:4212 | taken before a public officer;
-- src:4214 | (b) receive acknowledgements of recognisances of bail and
-- src:4215 | bail bonds;
-- src:4217 | (c) administer oaths for —
-- src:4219 | (i) the justification for bail;
-- src:4221 | (ii) taking any affidavit or affirmation;
-- src:4223 | (iii) receiving and taking the answer, plea, demurrer,
-- src:4224 | disclaimer, allegation or examination of any party or
-- src:4225 | parties to any action;
-- src:4227 | (iv) the examination of any witnesses upon any
-- src:4228 | interrogatories or de bene esse or in chief or on
-- src:4229 | any other occasions;
-- src:4231 | (v) swearing executors and administrators; and
-- src:4233 | (vi) swearing persons in any cause or matter which is
-- src:4234 | pending or about to be instituted in any court in any
-- src:4235 | of its jurisdiction;
-- src:4237 | (d) take and receive statutory declarations.
@ref s 68(2) (src:4205-4237)
GIVEN thing IS A `s 68(2) thing a commissioner for oaths may do`
      `the appointment expresses a limitation that excludes the thing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 68(2) the commissioner for oaths appointed by the Senate may do the thing` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "who may do all or any of the following things" does not close the list with "only"
    WHEN `s 68(2) another thing` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the appointment expresses a limitation that excludes the thing`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to any limitations expressed in their appointment" -- the limitation prevails and the subsection says nothing further
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 69 -- Oaths of officers`

DECLARE `s 69(1) party` IS ONE OF `s 69(1) the officer`
DECLARE `s 69(1) act` IS ONE OF `s 69(1) takes and subscribes the appropriate oath of office set out in the Second Schedule`

-- src:4247 | 69.—(1) The Registrar, the Deputy Registrar, the Assistant
-- src:4248 | Registrars and such other officers of the Supreme Court as may be
-- src:4249 | required by the Chief Justice must, before exercising the functions of
-- src:4256 | their respective offices, take and subscribe the appropriate oath of
-- src:4257 | office set out in the Second Schedule.
@ref s 69(1) (src:4247-4257)
GIVEN officer IS A `Officer of the Supreme Court`
      `the Chief Justice requires the officer to take the oath` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer has taken and subscribed an oath of office before exercising the functions of the office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sch 2 the oath taken is the appropriate oath of office set out in the Second Schedule` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 69(1) the officer has taken and subscribed the oath before exercising the functions of the office, as the section requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty binds the Registrar, the Deputy Registrar, the Assistant Registrars and "such other officers of the Supreme Court as may be required by the Chief Justice"
        IF NOT (officer EQUALS Registrar OR officer EQUALS `Deputy Registrar` OR officer EQUALS `Assistant Registrar` OR `the Chief Justice requires the officer to take the oath`) THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "must, before exercising the functions of their respective offices, take and subscribe" -- a bare "must" not done: no oath was taken, and the text states the duty and does not say what follows
        IF NOT `the officer has taken and subscribed an oath of office before exercising the functions of the office` THEN NOTHING
        -- the oath was taken: whether it was "the appropriate oath of office set out in the Second Schedule" is the answer of another part of this encoding (PLAN.md seam 18)
        OTHERWISE `sch 2 the oath taken is the appropriate oath of office set out in the Second Schedule`

-- src:4247 | 69.—(1) The Registrar, the Deputy Registrar, the Assistant
-- src:4248 | Registrars and such other officers of the Supreme Court as may be
-- src:4249 | required by the Chief Justice must, before exercising the functions of
-- src:4256 | their respective offices, take and subscribe the appropriate oath of
-- src:4257 | office set out in the Second Schedule.
@ref s 69(1) (src:4247-4257)
`s 69(1) the duty of the officer to take and subscribe the oath of office` MEANS
    PARTY `s 69(1) the officer`
    MUST `s 69(1) takes and subscribes the appropriate oath of office set out in the Second Schedule`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 69(1) the officer` BECAUSE "the officer exercised the functions of the office without taking and subscribing the appropriate oath of office"

#TRACE `s 69(1) the duty of the officer to take and subscribe the oath of office` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 69(1) the officer` DOES `s 69(1) takes and subscribes the appropriate oath of office set out in the Second Schedule` AT 1

DECLARE `s 69(2) way of taking the oath` IS ONE OF
    `s 69(2) through a live video link`
    `s 69(2) through a live television link`
    `s 69(2) in another way`

-- src:4261 | (2) To avoid doubt, where an oath of office is required to be taken
-- src:4262 | and subscribed under subsection (1), a person may take and subscribe
-- src:4263 | the oath by appearing before the person administering the oath
-- src:4264 | through a live video link or live television link created using a remote
-- src:4265 | communication technology that allows the person administering the
-- src:4266 | oath to —
-- src:4268 | (a) maintain visual contact and communicate with the person
-- src:4269 | taking the oath, and any interpreter present, throughout the
-- src:4270 | process;
-- src:4272 | (b) confirm the identity of the person taking the oath and any
-- src:4273 | interpreter present; and
-- src:4275 | (c) verify by inspection the oath to be subscribed.
@ref s 69(2) (src:4261-4275)
GIVEN `an oath of office is required to be taken and subscribed under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      way IS A `s 69(2) way of taking the oath`
      `the technology lets the person administering the oath maintain visual contact and communicate with the person taking the oath, and any interpreter present, throughout the process` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technology lets the person administering the oath confirm the identity of the person taking the oath and any interpreter present` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technology lets the person administering the oath verify by inspection the oath to be subscribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 69(2) the person may take and subscribe the oath by appearing before the person administering the oath through a live link` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where an oath of office is required to be taken and subscribed under subsection (1), a person may" -- the "where" is not met
        IF NOT `an oath of office is required to be taken and subscribed under subsection (1)` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection allows a live video link or a live television link; it does not say in terms that another way is not allowed
        IF way EQUALS `s 69(2) in another way` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the technology lets the person administering the oath maintain visual contact and communicate with the person taking the oath, and any interpreter present, throughout the process`
           AND `the technology lets the person administering the oath confirm the identity of the person taking the oath and any interpreter present`
           AND `the technology lets the person administering the oath verify by inspection the oath to be subscribed`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the link must be "created using a remote communication technology that allows" the three things in paragraphs (a), (b) and (c); the subsection does not say what follows if one is missing
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 70 -- Apportionment of work`

-- s 70 is inert (reason 2): the Chief Justice's power to make rules for the apportionment of work is rule-making machinery; no decision follows from it.

§§ `Division 5 -- Offices`

§§ `s 71 -- Registry of Supreme Court`

-- src:4291 | 71.—(1) There shall be an office of the Supreme Court called the
-- src:4292 | Registry comprising such departments as the Chief Justice may, from
-- src:4293 | time to time, determine.
@ref s 71(1) (src:4291-4293)
GIVEN `the Chief Justice has determined that the department forms part of the Registry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 71(1) the department is part of the Registry of the Supreme Court` MEANS
    IF `the Chief Justice has determined that the department forms part of the Registry`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Registry comprises "such departments as the Chief Justice may, from time to time, determine"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4295 | (2) The Registry is under the control and supervision of the
-- src:4296 | Registrar.
@ref s 71(2) (src:4295-4296)
GIVEN officer IS A `Officer of the Supreme Court`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 71(2) the officer has the control and supervision of the Registry` MEANS
    CONSIDER officer
    WHEN Registrar THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Registry is under the control and supervision of the Registrar"; the subsection does not say in terms that no one else shares it
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 72 -- Registry to be open throughout the year`

-- Saturday: 3 January 2026 is a Saturday (hand-checked against a calendar; 4 January 2026 is the Sunday the Interpretation Act module uses).
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 72(1) the day is a Saturday` d MEANS
    ((Day d) MODULO 7) EQUALS ((Day (Date 3 1 2026)) MODULO 7)

-- src:4300 | 72.—(1) The Registry of the Supreme Court is to be open on every
-- src:4301 | day of the year except on Saturdays, Sundays and public holidays.
@ref s 72(1) (src:4300-4301)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 72(1) the Registry of the Supreme Court is to be open on the day` d `the public holidays` MEANS
    IF `s 72(1) the day is a Saturday` d OR `is an excluded day` d `the public holidays`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is to be open on every day of the year except on Saturdays, Sundays and public holidays"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:4308 | (2) Despite subsection (1), the Registrar may lawfully sit or carry
-- src:4309 | out the business of the Registry on a Saturday, Sunday or public
-- src:4310 | holiday if —
-- src:4312 | (a) the Chief Justice has directed the Registrar to do so on that
-- src:4313 | day; or
-- src:4315 | (b) in the opinion of the Registrar, the business to be
-- src:4316 | despatched is extremely urgent.
@ref s 72(2) (src:4308-4316)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the Chief Justice has directed the Registrar to sit or carry out the business of the Registry on that day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the Registrar, the business to be despatched is extremely urgent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 72(2) the Registrar may lawfully sit or carry out the business of the Registry on the day` d `the public holidays` `the Chief Justice has directed the Registrar to sit or carry out the business of the Registry on that day` `in the opinion of the Registrar, the business to be despatched is extremely urgent` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday"; on another day subsection (1) has the Registry open and the subsection says nothing
        IF NOT (`s 72(1) the day is a Saturday` d OR `is an excluded day` d `the public holidays`) THEN NOTHING
        IF `the Chief Justice has directed the Registrar to sit or carry out the business of the Registry on that day` OR `in the opinion of the Registrar, the business to be despatched is extremely urgent` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may lawfully sit or carry out the business of the Registry on a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday if (a) ... or (b) ..." -- neither is met
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:4318 | (3) The office hours of the Registry are such times as the Chief
-- src:4319 | Justice may from time to time direct.
@ref s 72(3) (src:4318-4319)
GIVEN `the Chief Justice has directed the times` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 72(3) the times are the office hours of the Registry` MEANS
    IF `the Chief Justice has directed the times`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the office hours are "such times as the Chief Justice may from time to time direct"
    ELSE NOTHING
